From b09f9a30704626f961e4d8bb35ef1085e596c6b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 15:24:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] board: freescale: gateway-dk: add USB PD and EEPROM
 device programming
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the two heavier self-tests that not only probe their target but
also program persistent state when needed:

  - usbpd_controller.c (+ NVM_config_STUSB45.h):
        STUSB4500 USB PD controller. Reads NVM via the FTP register
        family (UM2650 §3), compares against the expected PDO
        configuration, and reprograms if mismatched. The chip is
        identified up-front via Device_ID register 0x2F.

  - eeprom.c:
        AT24CS32 board-info EEPROM (32 Kbit / 4 KB). Reads model,
        serial, and per-port MAC addresses, and exposes them as
        U-Boot environment variables (model, serial_number,
        ethaddr..eth4addr). Also provides the 'program_eeprom'
        u-boot command for factory provisioning.

Both probe through the same setup_i2c_muxed_device() helper as the
lighter tests in the previous patch, but their bodies are bigger
because they do real device-programming work.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific]

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
